        "original_id": "0ee90bbb-bee4-5e94-a667-f89c36d8ea3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lysichiton, Ageratum, Orontium, Symplocarpus\n- Taxonomy: Araceae, Asteraceae, Eupatorieae, Orontioideae\n- Places: North America, Asia, eastern North America, USA\n\nFacts:\n- Lysichiton is a plant genus in the family Araceae.\n- Ageratum is a plant genus of 40 to 60 tropical and warm temperate flowering annual and perennial species in the family Asteraceae and the tribe Eupatorieae.\n- In the USA, Ageratum is known as whiteweed.\n- The subfamily Orontioideae consists of three genera: Lysichiton, Orontium, and Symplocarpus.\n- Lysichiton includes one to two species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.\n- Orontium, known as golden club, has one living species from eastern North America and two extinct species known from fossils.\n- Symplocarpus includes several species of skunk cabbage from North America and Asia.",
